.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tensor-wasm-run 1  "tensor-wasm-run "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-run \- Run a Wasm module locally against the in\-process TensorWasm engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm run\fR [\fB\-\-export\fR=\fIEXPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-args\fR=\fIARGS\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Spawns a TensorWasmExecutor over a default TensorWasmEngine, instantiates the supplied \fB.wasm\fR file under TenantId(1), invokes the requested export (default \fBmain\fR), and prints \fBok\fR on success or the error chain otherwise.
.PP
Arguments destined for the guest are accepted as a JSON array via \fB\-\-args\fR; today the executor's call_export only supports the \fB() -> ()\fR signature, so non\-empty argument lists are validated then ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR=\fIEXPORT\fR [default: main]
Name of the exported function to call.
.TP
\fB\-\-args\fR=\fIARGS\fR
Arguments to pass to the export, encoded as a JSON array (e.g. \fB\(aq[1.0, 2.0]\(aq\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests (inherited from the top\-level flag).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Path to the \fB.wasm\fR file to execute.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
tensor\-wasm run tests/wasm\-fixtures/vector_add.wasm \-\-export add \-\-args \(aq[1.0, 2.0]\(aq
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-bench(1), tensor\-wasm\-invoke(1)
